// Package rangeslider renders Tabler's range slider with noUiSlider: one or several handles, a filled
// track between them, steps and a color (text-{color} on Class). With Name the values are submitted with
// the form, in hidden inputs. Load the plugin with Library in the head.
//
//	@rangeslider.Slider(rangeslider.Props{ID: "price", Name: "price", Values: []float64{60, 90}, Max: 100, Step: 10, Label: "Price range"})
package rangeslider

import (
	"strconv"

	"github.com/mind-vm/tabler-templ/internal/plugin"
	"github.com/mind-vm/tabler-templ/kit"
)

// Version is the noUiSlider version Library loads.
const Version = "15.8.1"

// LibraryURL and StylesheetURL are noUiSlider on jsDelivr.
const (
	LibraryURL    = "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/nouislider@" + Version + "/dist/nouislider.min.js"
	StylesheetURL = "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/nouislider@" + Version + "/dist/nouislider.min.css"
)

type Props struct {
	ID         string
	Name       string // submits the values in hidden inputs with this name
	Class      string // e.g. "text-green" for the color
	Attributes templ.Attributes
	Min        float64
	Max        float64 // default 100
	Step       float64 // default 1
	// Values are the handles, default one at 50.
	Values []float64
	// Connect fills the track before a single handle; several handles always fill between them.
	Connect bool
	Label   string // aria-label of the handles; with two, "… minimum" and "… maximum"
	// Settings are noUiSlider options merged over the built ones.
	Settings map[string]any
}

func (p Props) values() []float64 {
	if len(p.Values) == 0 {
		return []float64{50}
	}
	return p.Values
}

// options ports Tabler's Range.astro.
func (p Props) options() string {
	vs := p.values()
	o := map[string]any{"start": vs, "step": p.Step, "range": map[string]float64{"min": p.Min, "max": p.Max}}
	if p.Max == 0 {
		o["range"] = map[string]float64{"min": p.Min, "max": 100}
	}
	if p.Step == 0 {
		o["step"] = 1
	}
	if len(vs) > 1 || p.Connect {
		var c []bool
		for i := 2; i <= len(vs); i++ {
			c = append(c, (i-2)%2 != 0)
		}
		o["connect"] = append(c, true, false)
	}
	if p.Label != "" {
		labels := make([]map[string]string, len(vs))
		for i := range vs {
			l := p.Label
			switch {
			case len(vs) == 2 && i == 0:
				l += " minimum"
			case len(vs) == 2:
				l += " maximum"
			case len(vs) > 2:
				l += " handle " + strconv.Itoa(i+1)
			}
			labels[i] = map[string]string{"aria-label": l}
		}
		o["handleAttributes"] = labels
	}
	for k, v := range p.Settings {
		o[k] = v
	}
	return plugin.JSON(o)
}

// Slider is a range slider.
templ Slider(p Props) {
	<div
		class={ kit.Classes("form-range mb-2", p.Class) }
		if p.ID != "" {
			id={ p.ID }
		}
		data-tabler-range={ p.options() }
		{ p.Attributes... }
	></div>
	if p.Name != "" {
		for _, v := range p.values() {
			<input type="hidden" name={ p.Name } value={ strconv.FormatFloat(v, 'f', -1, 64) } data-tabler-range-value={ p.ID }/>
		}
	}
	@Script()
}

// Script starts the sliders; Slider renders it.
func Script() templ.Component {
	return plugin.Start("rangeslider", `function (root) {
		if (!window.noUiSlider) return;
		root.querySelectorAll('[data-tabler-range]').forEach(function (el) {
			if (el.noUiSlider) return;
			noUiSlider.create(el, JSON.parse(el.getAttribute('data-tabler-range')));
			var inputs = el.id ? document.querySelectorAll('input[data-tabler-range-value="' + el.id + '"]') : [];
			if (inputs.length) el.noUiSlider.on('change', function (values) {
				inputs.forEach(function (input, i) { input.value = parseFloat(values[i]); });
			});
		});
	}`)
}

// Library loads noUiSlider and its stylesheet and starts every slider on the page; put it in the head, before
// Tabler's stylesheet (Tabler's vendor styles override the plugin's).
templ Library() {
	@plugin.Stylesheet(StylesheetURL)
	@plugin.Script(LibraryURL)
	@Script()
}
